<title>GERMANY: TENNIS-PHILIPPOUSSIS HITS WORLD-RECORD ACE.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-PHILIPPOUSSIS HITS WORLD-RECORD ACE.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Mark Philippoussis served up a world record ace at the World Team Cup on Sunday.</p>
<p>Philippoussis sealed the first set of his match against Spain's Albert Costa with an ace which registered 229 kph, the fastest ever recorded.</p>
<p>It bettered the Australian's own mark of 228.5 kph set in Scottsdale, Arizona, in March.</p>
</text>
